WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.314 --> 00:00:03.806
(electronic music)

00:00:03.806 --> 00:00:06.180
- When I was first thinking
about transitioning,

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.818
I was concerned that I wasn't
going to be able to compete.

00:00:08.818 --> 00:00:10.611
What will fans and spectators say?

00:00:10.611 --> 00:00:12.677
What will it be like in the locker room?

00:00:12.677 --> 00:00:15.008
Trans athletes have to
think about all of that

00:00:15.008 --> 00:00:17.098
as well as will I even be able

00:00:17.098 --> 00:00:18.478
to play the sports that I love

00:00:18.478 --> 00:00:20.721
because of the policies that are in place?

00:00:20.721 --> 00:00:23.122
My name is Chris Mosier, and I
am the first transgender man

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:25.872
to make a men's U.S. National team.

00:00:30.877 --> 00:00:32.969
My sport is sprint duathlon.

00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:35.697
Duathlon is run, bike, run.

00:00:35.697 --> 00:00:38.180
When I first started
competing after transition,

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.579
no one really thought
that I would do well.

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:42.208
Everyone pretty much just wrote me off

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.240
because they looked at me and thought,

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.944
"Oh, he's a trans guy.

00:00:45.944 --> 00:00:49.533
"There's no way that he
can compete against men."

00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:52.101
Hearing people say that
really motivated me

00:00:52.101 --> 00:00:54.835
to work harder, to learn more,

00:00:54.835 --> 00:00:56.941
to be more dedicated to my training

00:00:56.941 --> 00:01:00.513
and try to be the strongest
competitor that I can be.

00:01:00.513 --> 00:01:01.513
(gentle instrumental music)

00:01:01.513 --> 00:01:04.196
Competing on Team USA is
a dream come true for me.

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:06.988
Although I'm on Team
USA, I will not be able

00:01:06.988 --> 00:01:09.385
to compete in the World
Championships in June

00:01:09.385 --> 00:01:13.586
with the policies that
are in place right now.

00:01:13.586 --> 00:01:15.490
At the world level, they follow

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.048
the international Olympic
Committee policies,

00:01:18.048 --> 00:01:20.931
and those policies say, 
"Trans athlete needs

00:01:20.931 --> 00:01:24.311
"to go through a full medical transition."

00:01:24.311 --> 00:01:27.570
And they define that
as full lower surgery,

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:32.006
so including internal and
external genital reassignment.

00:01:32.006 --> 00:01:33.755
Adding an extra body part is not going

00:01:33.755 --> 00:01:37.379
to make me a faster runner
or a stronger cyclist.

00:01:37.379 --> 00:01:40.381
Every single day, I'm thinking about being

00:01:40.381 --> 00:01:42.288
on the starting line, and I really think

00:01:42.288 --> 00:01:43.507
that it's going to happen.

00:01:43.507 --> 00:01:46.321
I really believe that we
can get policy changed

00:01:46.321 --> 00:01:49.155
and that I will line up with my teammates

00:01:49.155 --> 00:01:51.322
in the red, white and blue uniform

00:01:51.322 --> 00:01:53.110
and represent my country.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.097
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:01:55.097 --> 00:01:56.603
Every day I read a quote that says

00:01:56.603 --> 00:01:58.874
"Be who you needed when you were younger."

00:01:58.874 --> 00:02:02.304
That puts me in the
mindset of sharing my story

00:02:02.304 --> 00:02:03.928
and making sure that people see me

00:02:03.928 --> 00:02:07.177
as a visibly out trans athlete competing

00:02:07.177 --> 00:02:10.007
at a high level so that they know

00:02:10.007 --> 00:02:12.174
that they can do that too.

